  <main id="main" class="legal-page section-pad"><article class="container prose"><span class="section-kicker">Privacy notice</span><h1>A small form with a clear boundary.</h1><p class="legal-date">Last updated: August 24, 2026</p><h2>About this concept</h2><p>Project Handoff is a fictional portfolio concept created by Joshua Carl Pelotea to demonstrate landing-page design, frontend implementation, form handling, accessibility, SEO, and consent-aware analytics.</p><h2>Information the form collects</h2><p>The waitlist form asks for a work email address, a team-size range, a primary workflow challenge, and consent to be contacted. Netlify processes the form submission so the concept’s conversion flow can be tested in production.</p><h2>Analytics</h2><p>Analytics is denied by default. If you explicitly opt in, GA4 may receive page views and interaction events such as CTA placement, form start, form error, and successful sign-up. Email addresses, form answers, team-size selections, and workflow selections are never sent to GA4.</p><h2>Purpose and retention</h2><p>Submission data is used only to demonstrate and validate the portfolio project. Do not submit confidential or sensitive information. Test submissions may be removed after functional verification.</p><h2>Your choice</h2><p>You can use the page without enabling analytics. Your analytics preference is saved in local browser storage and can be changed by clearing site data.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For questions or removal requests, email <a href="mailto:jcpelotea.business@gmail.com">jcpelotea.business@gmail.com</a>.</p><a class="button" href="/#waitlist">Return to the waitlist</a></article></main>
  <footer class="site-footer"><div class="container footer__bottom"><span>© 2026 Project Handoff concept</span><a href="/">Home</a></div></footer>
</SiteLayout>
